  "summary": [
    "Batch B, family B10 (genuine sequence cycles): the eight helpers whose body is MathComp's `ucycle r c` / `ucycleb r c` with the length guard `2 < size c`: SEVEN Prop helpers and ONE Boolean. Five Prop helpers read `ucycle (--) c /\\ 2 < size c` on simple graphs (Chromatic XE1 `xe1_cycle`, Cycle X9 `x9_genuine_cycle`, Cycle XE1 `xe1_cycle`, Extremal XE2 `xe2_cycle`, GTMisc X113 `x113_is_cycle`); two read the generic `ucycle r c /\\ 2 < size c` over an ARBITRARY supplied relation on a finite carrier (GTMisc XE1 `xe1_rel_cycle`, and the eighth source Digraph XE2 `xe2_directed_cycle`, an orientation, accepted into scope by the coordinator); X212's `x212_cycle` is the Boolean `ucycleb (--) c && (2 < size c)`. They now unfold to `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_cycle r c` / `seq_cycleb r c`, convertible, with the Prop/Boolean signatures unchanged; the generic interface adds no symmetry or looplessness. API: reflect adapter, projections, degenerate rejections (empty, singleton even with a loop, digon even with both directions), the triangle characterisation, repeats, rotation, cyclic consecutiveness, and reversal: a cycle of the converse relation in general, and of the same relation under the hypothesis `symmetric r`, a sufficient condition (a directed 3-cycle is grounded not to reverse).",
    "",
    "Seventeen rows and sixteen intermediates, frozen with this family's helpers only: Chromatic XE2 #58, #751, #1091 (odd cycles with diagonals, odd/separated cycle lengths); Cycle X212 Smith, Bondy (cyclic edge connectivity) and Birmele; Cycle X9 (two rows); Cycle XE1 #184; Cycle XE2 #641, #71, #752, #815 (cycle lengths); Extremal XE2 #767 (incident chords); GTMisc X113 (coarse Erdos-Posa); GTMisc XE1 #883 (coprime graph); Digraph XE2 #1006 (orientations). Every guard, constant, status and documented defect is unchanged. `xe2_distinct_cycle_lengths_at_least` (Cycle XE2) reaches the family but no row; it stays live and converts.",
    "",
    "History (complete `original-statement` rows; earlier partial snapshots unchanged): B1's X113 chain -> `X113Original` (B1 frozen pairwise distance and vertex set with this family's frozen cycle); B4's chromatic diagonal chain and A5's erdos_1091 / erdos_58 rows -> `XE2Original` erdos_1091 (A5 frozen subgraph helper, B4 frozen diagonal count, this family's frozen cycle) and erdos_58 (A5 frozen subgraph helper, this family's frozen odd cycle lengths); B4's X9 chord chain -> `X9Original`; B4's extremal incident-chord chain -> `XE2Original` #767. The Originals are certified through the earlier families' own certificates by conversion. Family A7 (edge counts) is not integrated: whichever of A7 / B10 integrates second composes the shared rows (#767).",
    "",
    "Kernel evidence, independent of this textual report: `Print All Dependencies` of every frozen statement and Original contains no live helper or chain of this family and neither `seq_cycle` nor `seq_cycleb`; the Originals also reach no live B1/B4/A5 helper or canonical; each live statement reaches the canonical and its alias (/srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/B10-genuine_cycle/print_all_dependencies_summary.txt).",
    "",
    "Baseline 00d6bb3 is a private, not-for-integration merge of B9 299dc71 with main 0659592 (A5, A6, B7, C6), conflicts only in _CoqProject lines (de-duplicated union) and simple_path.md (regenerated); no .v file differs from both parents. No statement text, doc block, manifest row or leg state changes (checked below).",
    "Later migration: Cycle X9 `x9_cycle_edges`, listed here as a separate raw cyclic edge list, was migrated by B11 (family cycle-edges) onto `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_cycle_edge_list`; it is no longer an untouched distinct variant.",
    "Later migration: Cycle X212 `x212_cycle_vertices`, listed here as a separate raw cycle vertex set, was migrated by B12 (family cycle-vertices) onto B1's `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_vertices`; it is no longer an untouched distinct variant.",
    "Later migration: Hom U3 `longest_cycle`, listed here as a separate enriched contract, was migrated by B13 (family longest-cycle) onto `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_longest_cycle`, a longest genuine cycle built on this family's `seq_cycleb`, through its all-ucycle and3 view; it is no longer an untouched distinct variant."
  ],
